---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} crumbs={[{href:'/guides/',label:'Guides'}]} current={title} article={{title,description,datePublished:'2026-10-15'}} cta={false}>
<article class="growth-article">
<header><p class="eyebrow">Budget planning</p><h1>What does a China factory visit cost?</h1><p class="lead">The budget depends on where your suppliers are, what you need to check and the support you book. Compare the same scope before comparing prices.</p><p class="meta">Prepared by ChinaFactoryHost · 15 October 2026</p></header>
<nav class="jump-links" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#budget">Budget items</a><a href="#scenarios">Trip scenarios</a><a href="#quote">Request a quote</a></nav>
<section id="budget"><h2>Build the budget in separate parts</h2><p>This is a planning worksheet, not a published rate card. Request a written quote for your dates and route; do not assume every item below is included in a daily fee.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Costs to confirm before booking</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What changes the cost</th><th scope="col">Ask the provider</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Planning and appointments</th><td>Existing shortlist or new supplier research; number of sites; access requirements.</td><td>Does the fee include supplier research and appointment confirmation, or only the visit day?</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Local transport</th><td>Factory addresses, vehicle size, waiting time, parking and intercity travel.</td><td>Are the driver, tolls, parking and overtime included?</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Interpreting and on-site support</th><td>Language, technical vocabulary, working hours and meeting scope.</td><td>Who will attend, for how long, and how is extra time charged?</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Your travel</th><td>Flights or trains, hotel location, nights away and local transfers.</td><td>Which bookings do you make yourself? Is staff travel charged separately?</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Samples and follow-up</th><td>Sample purchases, shipping, records, translation and additional supplier contact.</td><td>What written output is included? Which later tasks require a separate quote?</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Specialist work</th><td>Formal audits, laboratory tests or product inspections.</td><td>Is a separate specialist needed, and who quotes that work?</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="scenarios"><h2>Two routes can mean very different budgets</h2><div class="two-up"><article><h3>One region, confirmed suppliers</h3><p>Your shortlist and production addresses are already confirmed. Budget for the agreed local support, travel between sites and enough time for records. Check whether preliminary document review is included.</p></article><article><h3>Multiple cities, suppliers still being selected</h3><p>Allow for research, appointment changes, intercity travel and overnight stays. Price each travel leg and working day separately so that moving between cities does not hide inside the visit allowance.</p></article></div><p>These are planning scenarios, not customer case studies or quoted packages. Use the <a href="/guides/how-to-plan-a-china-factory-visit/">visit planning guide</a> to decide how much can fit into a day.</p></section>
<section class="note"><h2>Compare the total scope</h2><p>For each quote, record the currency, covered dates, working hours, transport, written deliverables, exclusions, payment schedule and cancellation or rescheduling terms. A lower daily rate may cover fewer tasks.</p><p>Keep a separate allowance for changes you have not priced. Agree how additional work will be approved before it starts.</p></section>
<section id="quote"><h2>What to send for a useful quote</h2><ol><li>Product and the decision you need the visit to support.</li><li>Supplier names and production addresses, or a request for help building a shortlist.</li><li>Preferred dates, visitor numbers and starting city.</li><li>Language, technical topics and any filming or access needs.</li><li>The records, samples or follow-up you want after the visit.</li></ol><p>If an address or appointment is unconfirmed, say so. That uncertainty affects both the route and the price.</p><p><a href="/contact/">Send your visit brief</a></p></section>
<div class="related"><a href="/factory-visits/">Factory visit support</a><a href="/tools/factory-visit-scorecard/">Compare suppliers after your visits</a></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
